{"chunk_id": "e8e6c86053ac", "text": "Parasurama, the formidable Brahmin-warrior who once exterminated the Kshatriya class to avenge his father Jamadagni, confronts Rama after hearing of the breaking of Shiva\u2019s bow. He presents the bow of Vishnu\u2014its divine counterpart\u2014and challenges Rama to string it. Rama calmly accepts. With controlled anger he effortlessly seizes the bow, strings it, and sets a divine arrow that cannot be withdrawn without fulfilling its purpose. The act shakes the three worlds and draws the gods to witness the moment. Realizing Rama\u2019s true nature, Parasurama recognizes him as Vishnu incarnate and submits. Rather than kill the sage, Rama strips him of the glory and power gained through austerities, forcing him to withdraw to Mount Mahendra. The episode marks the symbolic transfer of divine warrior authority from the old avataric hero to Rama.\nRama effortlessly strings Vishnu\u2019s bow, humbles Parasurama, and strips him of his glory, forcing the warrior-sage to acknowledge Rama\u2019s divine supremacy.\nThemes: divine recognition, humbling of pride, transfer of power, avatar of Vishnu, kshatriya dharma", "vector": [0.002054286887869239, -0.03003884293138981, -0.013815418817102909, 0.017304984852671623, -0.010992474853992462, 0.02069251798093319, -0.020624496042728424, -0.02133193239569664, -0.024760277941823006, -0.022842036560177803, 0.00737366545945406, -0.0054826331324875355, 0.004958857782185078, 0.008087904192507267, -0.002124010119587183, -0.002016874263063073, 0.041004110127687454, -0.02463783696293831, 0.040187835693359375, -0.0182437002658844, 0.01293112337589264, -0.01597174070775509, -0.015509185381233692, 0.018447767943143845, -0.02210739068686962, 0.010060563683509827, 0.009795274585485458, -0.02654247358441353, 0.018175676465034485, -0.02442016452550888, 0.0010968666756525636, -0.004778597503900528, -0.0002752795408014208, -0.0064111435785889626, -0.0263248011469841, -0.01234612800180912, 0.0023093721829354763,